    <!-- Subscription settings section (PayCraftPlanSection).
         These are the FALLBACKS for the dashboard-driven settings_* copy (migration 156): the SDK
         renders a tenant's value when they set one and these when they have not, so a tenant who
         never opens the paywall designer still gets localised wording rather than English baked
         into the server.

         The three templates use {days}/{date} rather than %1$s, matching the token convention the
         server columns use — one substitution path for both layers instead of two. The one-day form
         is its own string because no token can pluralise; "Trial — 1 days left" is the bug that
         ships when a count is always routed through one template.

         Manage / Upgrade / Restore deliberately reuse the existing paywall strings: an app should
         not say "Restore Your Premium" on the paywall and "Restore purchases" in settings. -->
